# Far copy, step 26.2 (7.2.44): the space A without an answerer. One program of language 3, nothing new: data, copy, emit, halt.
# A copies 8 bits four times (four different values, one after another) from its memory into the channel stdout (S+2); the shell
# connects this stdout to the stdin of the space B (far_b.tw). A reads nothing and waits for nothing: the channel is a copy of a byte.
:v0 data 8 165
:v1 data 8 60
:v2 data 8 1
:v3 data 8 200
:main block
emit &v0
emit &v1
emit &v2
emit &v3
halt
